  "final_answer": "All four deliverables are written to `/app` and verified.\n\n**Key judgments applied from HLF-7:**\n- **Scope (\u00a71):** 6 items out (3 `standalone_graphic`, 2 `vehicle_wrap` + COL-55) \u2014 not audited, not counted against allowance. A `temporary_banner` is installed signage \"for every purpose,\" so a permit covering `installed_signage` also covers banners \u2014 this clears 9 banners (e.g. COL-06) that a literal type-string read would pull, and it's what pushes ZN-01 to 60.5 sq ft (just over its 60.0 allowance).\n- **Permit (\u00a72):** followed `supersedes` chains to the last row \u2014 so items naming PMT-1004/1005 are governed by PMT-1006 (ZN-03 only), and PMT-1007 by PMT-1008 (expired 2026-08-19). Permits ending **on** 2026-08-20 (PMT-1002, PMT-1011) are still current.\n- **\u00a75 \u2192 \u00a76:** 5 zones breach allowance (ZN-01, ZN-02, ZN-03, ZN-07, ZN-08), triggering heightened inspection, which tightens the size cap by 1 sq ft in those zones only \u2014 newly making 7 items oversize. \u00a72/\u00a73/\u00a75 unchanged.\n\n**Batch figures:** collateral_count 60, permit_missing 11, egress 8, oversize 15, compliant 28, flagged 32, finding_total 34, out_of_scope 6, pulled 11, zones_over_allowance 5.",
